+"""🧬 CROSS-REFERENCE ENGINE :: Hermes 90k+ Skills Hub ⇄ DBAL ⇄ memory vault.
+
+Backend middleware only — the Mission Control frontend UI is never touched.
+
+What it does
+------------
+1. **Unified 90k+ Hermes hub cross-referencing.**  A deterministic
+   ``agentskills.io``-style catalogue (204 categories × 442 skills =
+   90 168 skills) is materialised into a local SQLite **DBAL index**
+   (``~/.omnihack/vault/hermes_hub.db``) and deep-linked with the local
+   skill registry, the MCP tool gateway, GitHub repo templates
+   (``awesome-llm-apps`` family) and historical execution logs from the
+   memory vault.
+
+2. **Progressive disclosure / zero bloat.**  The 90k rows are *never*
+   loaded at once.  A tiny in-memory "yellow pages" (one token-set per
+   category, ~204 entries) is scored first; only the top categories are
+   then fetched from SQLite with ``LIMIT``.  ``materialize()`` returns
+   exactly the one script/reference/tool-hook a sub-task needs.
+
+3. **Autonomous skill evolution (closed loop).**  When a daemon or
+   sub-agent completes a multi-step task, ``evolve_skill(trace)`` fuses the
+   execution trace into a new custom skill, validates it against evaluation
+   gates, and persists it to ``~/.hermes/skills/``.
+
+4. **120 s DBAL sync daemon.**  A background thread flushes cross-referenced
+   execution data into the DBAL on the same 120 s heartbeat used by the
+   API-NEXUS worker.
+
+Everything is local & deterministic — no network is required for the app to
+run natively.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import hashlib
+import json
+import os
+import random
+import re
+import sqlite3
+import threading
+import time
+from typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional
+
